OL,3,AClose-up images to be revealed of
OL,4,Aasteroid deliberately hit to test
OL,5,Aability to protect Earth
OL,6,
OL,7,FPictures will be released later of
OL,8,Fdamage to an asteroid that was
OL,9,Fdeliberately hit with a spacecraft four
OL,10,Fyears ago as part of a test of Earth's
OL,11,Fdefences.
OL,13,FIn what may sound like the plot of a
OL,14,Fdisaster movie, Nasa's Dart spacecraft
OL,15,Fsmashed into the space rock in 2022 to
OL,16,Fknock it slightly off course.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11914
SC,0014
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1795627138
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AClose-up images to be revealed of
OL,4,Aasteroid deliberately hit to test
OL,5,Aability to protect Earth
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe Nasa craft was obliterated on
OL,8,Fimpact. Now, a European Space Agency
OL,9,F(ESA) mission called Hera is scouring
OL,10,Fthe scene to fully assess the aftermath
OL,11,Fof the collision - with the first
OL,12,Fimages set to be released later on
OL,13,FWednesday.
OL,15,FThe asteroid poses no threat. Instead,
OL,16,Fthis was the first ever test of our
OL,17,Fplanetary defences to see what action
OL,18,Fwe could take if a space rock were
OL,19,Fheading for our planet.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/39
